Go toolchain

Install:
  Install the latest stable Go release when the managed toolchain is absent; verify downloaded archives and repair missing command links and GOBIN configuration.

Upgrade:
  Update the installed managed toolchain to the latest stable release; verify downloaded archives and repair missing command links and GOBIN configuration.

Status:
  Report the managed Go command location and version, or the Go command on PATH when the managed command is unavailable.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.
  Supported architectures: amd64 and arm64.

Configuration:
  Destination: ~/.local/share/go
  The current symlink selects the managed release; previous release directories are retained.
  Back up the current link only when selecting a different release, then publish the new link atomically.
  Missing command links are created in ~/.local/bin; existing user entry points are preserved.
  GOBIN defaults to ~/.local/bin only when unset; existing values are preserved.
  GOENV must allow persistent Go configuration.
  Changed GOENV files are staged and renamed into place; symbolic links are backed up and replaced without modifying their targets.
  Open a new terminal after installation to load environment changes.
